body:
### Tested versions

Tested in 4.4 Stable, 4.4.1 Stable, 4.5 Beta 5

### System information

Windows 10 - NVIDIA GTX 750 Ti Driver version: 580.97 - Vulkan(Mobile/Forward+))

### Issue description

When using Godot 4.4+ with the Vulkan backend(Forward+ or mobile) on a GTX 750 Ti GPU, layering a TileMapLayer with a shader (using a sampler2D uniform) on top of another TileMapLayer triggers the following error during runtime and crashes the game:
```
E 0:00:01:850 fence_wait: Condition "err != VK_SUCCESS" is true. Returning: FAILED
<...> rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp:2439 @ fence_wait()
```

This only occurs when:
- Using the Vulkan renderer.
- The shader includes a texture sampler (overlay_tex).
- The shader-bearing TileMapLayer is rendered on top of another TileMapLayer in the scene.
- The TileMapLyer with the shader has at least one tile.

The issue disappears when:
- Using the Compatibility renderer (OpenGL).
- Using older verison of Godot
- The shader-only layer is rendered beneath other layers.
- Using the TileMap node with multiple layers.
- The layer is tested alone (no other overlapping TileMap layers).

To my knowledge the GTX 750 Ti is Vulkan capable and conformant (Vulkan 1.2). My drivers are updated and since the error doesnt show up any other time its possibly a bug but it could just be the gpu being too old i dont know.

**Expected behavior:**
Overlay shader layer should render cleanly, without Vulkan sync errors.

The shader i was using:
```glsl
shader_type canvas_item;

uniform sampler2D overlay_tex: repeat_enable, filter_nearest;
uniform float scale = 0.006944444; // calculated by 1/texture size e.g. 1/144
varying vec2 world_position;

void vertex(){
	// calculate the world position for use in the fragment shader
    world_position = (MODEL_MATRIX * vec4(VERTEX, 0.0, 1.0)).xy;
}

void fragment() {
	// only apply overlay_tex on the fully red parts of the original tiles
	float mix_amount = floor(COLOR.r);

	// sample the overlay_tex using worldPos
	vec4 overlay_color = texture(overlay_tex, world_position * scale);

	// combine original color and overlay color together
	COLOR = mix(COLOR, overlay_color, mix_amount);
}
```
### Steps to reproduce

1. Create two TileMapLayer nodes stacked.
2. Apply a shader to the top layer that samples from `sampler2D overlay_tex`.
3. Run the project using Vulkan renderer.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[vulkan_error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21736939/vulkan_error.zip)
